Psyche’s “year” - orbital period is how long it takes Psyche to orbit the sun.
Its orbital period compared to Earth is 4.99 Earth years

Psyche’s “day” - rotational period is how long Psyche takes to complete one full rotation.
Its rotational period is about 4.2 Earth hours.

Conversion of Earth days to Psyche Days:

 We must calculate how many Psyche days are in an Earth period.


Psyche Days = Earth Days x 24 / Rotation Period of Psyche in hours = 24/4.2= Earth Days x 5.71


With the given information above, for every Earth Day, there are about 5.71 Psyche Days.

Conversion of Earth Years to Psyche Years: 

Since Psyche takes about 4.99 Earth years to complete an orbit around the Sun. To convert between Earth Years and Psyche Years we must divide the 4.99 by the Earth Years.


Psyche Years = Earth Years / 4.99

	We can also go from Psyche Years to Earth Years:

Earth Years = Psyche Years x 4.99

Example conversion of Earth to Psyche Time:
Convert Earth Days to Psyche Days:
10 Earth Days x 5.71 = 57.1 Psyche Days


Convert Earth Years to Psyche Years

2 Earth Years ÷ 4.99 = 0.4 Psyche Years

 

